			"Message": "build(Land): Add diagnostics overlay and generated-artifact clean script\n\nAdd a new `.env.Land.Diagnostics` overlay exposing debug-only knobs: Inspect (WKWebView DevTools), Smoke (CommandCatalog test harness), Trace (dev-log tag selection), Record (dev-log file sink), and Disable (master kill-switch to bypass all Land customisations).\n\nShip `.env.Land.Diagnostics.Sample` as the canonical comment block; TierEnvironment.sh now sources the new overlay after PostHog.\n\nAdd `Maintain/Script/CleanGenerated.sh` to wipe source-side generated artefacts (Wind/Cocoon/Sky codegen, tonic-prost output, proto mtimes) that `cargo:rerun-if-changed` can't detect when `Generated/` is deleted by hand. Build.sh sources this helper when Clean=true.\n\nSync Element submodule to latest downstream versions which add Disable=true for bisecting typing/input regressions and refine Output/Sky with CSP loosening, icon URL fixes, and input routing options.\n\nThis enables developers to bisect whether regressions originate in Land's customizations or upstream/Tauri/WKWebView by running with Disable=true.",
			"SHA": "11c3c5905596a97db0349cd8d27c65ccd111b05f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T20:27:51Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				107,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Sync submodule updates with macOS UX fixes and extension webview support\n\nSynchronize five Element submodules to their latest downstream versions delivering critical macOS UX improvements and extension webview infrastructure:\n- Mountain: Fix boot race and close handling for macOS (Cmd+W intercept, DevTools focus opt-in) and add vscode-webview:// URI scheme handler for extension webviews (Roo Code, Claude, GitLens)\n- Output: Add macOS titlebar offset and z-index CSS transforms, expand sandbox stripping to both iframe sites, rewrite webview shell CSP\n- Sky: Add window close handler (Cmd+W closes active editor first), lifecycle focus after restoration, and opt-in command catalog smoke test\n- Wind: Update service layer with latest Effect-TS changes\n\nThese fixes resolve the \"I can't type or keybind\" issue, empty Explorer on first launch, and enable sideloaded extension webviews to render properly.",
			"SHA": "b03e792bcab717d62f36fa3211adfc37e9e147cb"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T18:59:51Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				107,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Sync submodule updates with dependency bumps and Mountain extension roots\n\nSynchronize seven Element submodules to their latest downstream versions:\n- Cocoon: Bump OpenTelemetry devDependencies (sdk-trace-node, exporter-trace-otlp-http, sdk-trace-base, sdk-logs, sdk-metrics, sdk-trace-web)\n- Common: Bump @cloudflare/workers-types to 4.20260430.1\n- Echo: Bump @cloudflare/workers-types to 4.20260430.1\n- Mountain: Revert to simple Mountain naming and add extension_root allowlist for Land and VSCode extension directories\n- Wind: Bump OpenTelemetry devDependencies and reformat ESBuild config/output to readable multi-line format\n- Worker: Bump @types/serviceworker and expand ESBuild configuration from minified to readable format\n- Output: Sync point\n\nThe Mountain extension_root allowlist enables the `/Extension/<abs-fs-path>` URL prefix to serve extension-contributed assets (icons, webview resources) from ~/.land/extensions and ~/.vscode/extensions, fixing missing icons for sideloaded extensions like GitLens.",
			"SHA": "9b8bab2887f5ff3ffe183f2525292c3f648618a6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T05:25:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				107,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Element): Sync submodule with Cocoon codegen entry point\n\nSynchronize Element submodule to include Cocoon's completed codegen infrastructure:\n- Codegen.ts: Runnable CLI entry point invoked by prepublishOnly.sh build hook\n- Resolves source/output paths from process.cwd() pointing to VS Code editor source tree and Cocoon output directory\n- Handles exit codes: non-zero for internal failures, exit code 2 for codegen failures, clean exit with summary on success\n- index.ts: Public module exports including RunExtHostCodegen orchestrator and options/summary types, IterateExtHostDecorators async iterator and IsExtHostFile predicate, EmitExtHostSchema emitter with options/outcome types, and ExtHostDecoratorRecord type\n\nThis completes the extension-host codegen pipeline added in the previous commit, making it callable from the build system.",
			"SHA": "e4fdcef414751c0ce96d4e2328774e4203360b3f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T05:23:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				107,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Element): Sync submodule with extension-host codegen and bridge shape generation\n\nSynchronize three Element submodules to their latest downstream versions delivering Phase-3 codegen pipeline completion:\n\n- Cocoon: Add extension-host codegen infrastructure mirroring Wind's ServiceSchema codegen but targeting the extHost decorator family. Extract/IsExtHostFile.ts filters to vs/workbench/api/*/extHost*.ts, IterateExtHostDecorators.ts resolves cross-file interfaces and records paired MainThread counterparts, EmitExtHostSchema.ts emits schema files under Cocoon/Source/Effect/Generated/<Decorator>/, and RunExtHostCodegen.ts orchestrates the pipeline.\n\n- Mountain: Rename binary and library to verbose production profile name (ProductionNodeEnvironment_MicrosoftVSCodeDependency_22NodeVersion_Bundle_Clean_Compile_ElectronProfile_EsbuildCompiler_Mountain). Update tauri.conf.json productName and identifier, and add duplicate Binary/node entry to externalBin for production node path. Supports multi-profile build pipeline.\n\n- Wind: Phase-3 codegen pipeline adds bridge shape generation - EmitBridgeShape.ts generates Pick<...Upstream, ...> bridge shape files derived from codegen-emitted upstream schemas, eliminating hand-maintained bridge shapes. WorkbenchBridgeShapeManifest provides curated narrowing of 18 upstream members per service. Also adds WorkbenchProductService and WorkbenchProgressService. prepublishOnly.sh now runs codegen before production build.",
			"SHA": "299b6a328a955cf836659b013cbb26fcec7cb7b5"
		}
